<p>Use the following procedure to divide a document into chapters and print 
 the first page of each chapter on different paper. You can also specify 
 a special print mode for the first page of each chapter. (Designate/Chapter)<br/>
In addition, you can print the selected pages on different paper. (Designated 
 Sheet Print)</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you use, this function may not be available.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver you are using.</p>
<h2>Changing the Print Mode for the First Page of Each Chapter</h2>
<ol>
<li><p>Create a document containing several chapters 
 in your application and open the printing preferences dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Cover/Slip/Designate</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Designate/Chapter</span> 
 check box. </p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span>.<br/>
 The <a href="~/Topics/idh_ddesignate"><span class="Term-Soft">Designate/Chapter 
 Details</span></a> dialog box appears.</p></li>
<li><p>In <span class="Term-Soft">Page Number:</span>, 
 enter the page number on which a new chapter begins.<br/>
 You can specify multiple page numbers for multiple new chapters by 
 inserting commas between the page numbers.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">If you use 
 the application to configure print settings such as page range, odd/even 
 pages only, or page layout, it is likely that this function's page numbering 
 will be affected. For instance, if the document contains 60 pages but 
 in the application you have specified the page range as 41 to 60, the 
 printer will print pages 1 to 20.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="6">
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Mode:</span> 
 list, select the <a class="help-popup-link" data-help-popup="true" href="~/Topics/PCL_CS/IDH_CCHAPTER">print mode</a> 
 for the page specified in <span class="Term-Soft">Page Number:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span> 
 list, select the input tray containing the media type to use for the chapter 
 page.</p></li>
<li><p>Specify the type of printing medium you want to 
 use in <span class="Term-Soft">Paper Type in Bypass Tray:</span> when using 
 bypass tray paper as the chapter page.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Add</span> to add 
 your definitions of <span class="Term-Soft">Page Number:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Mode:</span>, and <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span> to <span class="Term-Soft">Designate/Chapter 
 Settings List:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>If necessary, make settings for other chapters. 
 The maximum numbers of chapter covers you can specify differs depending 
 on the printer you are using.</p></li>
<li><p>When you have completed defining all chapter pages, 
 review the lists in <span class="Term-Soft">Designate/Chapter Settings List:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>To make modifications, select the item and make 
 corrections in the settings. Click <span class="Term-Soft">Modify</span> 
 after completing the corrections.</p></li>
<li><p>To delete an unnecessary item, click <span class="Term-Soft">Delete</span> 
 after selecting the one in the list.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2>Printing the Selected Pages on Different Paper</h2>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Depending on the printer you use, the Designate/Chapter 
 function is unavailable.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Create a document containing several chapters 
 in your application and open the printing preferences dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Cover/Slip/Designate</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Designate/Chapter</span> 
 check box. </p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span>.<br/>
 The <a href="~/Topics/idh_ddesignate"><span class="Term-Soft">Designate/Chapter 
 Details</span></a> dialog box appears.</p></li>
<li><p>In <span class="Term-Soft">Page Number:</span>, 
 enter the range of pages to specify a new chapter by inserting a hyphen 
 between the page numbers.<br/>
 You can specify multiple page numbers for multiple new chapters by 
 inserting commas between the page numbers.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">If you use 
 the application to configure print settings such as page range, odd/even 
 pages only, or page layout, it is likely that this function's page numbering 
 will be affected. For instance, if the document contains 60 pages but 
 in the application you have specified the page range as 41 to 60, the 
 printer will print pages 1 to 20.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="6">
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Mode:</span> 
 list, select <span class="Term-Soft">Designated Sheet Print</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span> 
 list, select the input tray containing the media type to use for the specified 
 range of pages.</p></li>
<li><p>Specify the type of printing medium you want to 
 use in <span class="Term-Soft">Paper Type in Bypass Tray:</span> when using 
 bypass tray paper for the specified range of pages.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Add</span> to add 
 your definitions of <span class="Term-Soft">Page Number:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Mode:</span>, and <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span> to <span class="Term-Soft">Designate/Chapter 
 Settings List:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>If necessary, make settings for other chapters. 
 The maximum numbers of chapters you can specify differs depending on the 
 printer you are using.</p></li>
<li><p>When you have completed defining all chapter pages, 
 review the lists in <span class="Term-Soft">Designate/Chapter Settings List:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>To make modifications, select the item and make 
 corrections in the settings. Click <span class="Term-Soft">Modify</span> 
 after completing the corrections.</p></li>
<li><p>To delete an unnecessary item, click <span class="Term-Soft">Delete</span> 
 after selecting the one in the list.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
